  "executions": 36,
  "finding": "Inference and training behave differently and the contract currently treats them the same. All 6 inference workloads are bit-identical across 5 seeds and both backends, so single-run acceptance is sound for them. Both training workloads swept have a seed spread larger than their margin to the effective threshold, and in both the verdict flips: a recorded pass (graph node classification) misses under seed 1, and a recorded miss (time-series forecasting) passes under seed 7. A single accepted run therefore does not determine a training verdict.",
  "note": "Every case is an inference workload evaluating a pinned checkpoint over a fixed set. None consumed the seed and none varied by backend. Training workloads are not covered here and are not claimed to be seed-invariant.",
  "purpose": "Quality determinism across seeds and execution backends. The registry sets acceptance_runs: 1 for quality, which is only defensible if the quality metric does not vary run to run. This measures whether it does.",
